A||N||12||1FST2M6||Picking a fight with a 72 Monte Carlo||||1||
Z||000000||1FST2M6||09-06-2001||09:02 AM||||out on the local strip last night messing around since i've finally got my car on the road and am really able to pick a fight. just met a baby crap green 72 Monte Carlo at a light under I-75. he's pointing and laughing and ask "<B>HEY</B>... it's noisy but bet it can't pull a string out of a gnats A$$" more snickering and taunting. all i said was "Pony up buddy" he just laughed a bit more and said "ok, man". as the traffic cleared the intersection the light droped green and i eased in the throttle and once rolling i nailed the nitrous I pulled him the next 3 lights he was back about 2-3 car lenghts by the first light (1/16 mi) and probly 4 or 5 by the time we hit the next stop light.. he and his passenger were all dangling out the passenger window.. "<B>WHAT THE HELL IS THAT?</B>"  i just told him "a 2.8 automatic and a little nitrous! what cha got?" he said "uum a 400 / turbo 400 and a 3:73. a little more on the way.. lets try that again." me feeling rather confident "ok lets try that one more time."  well the dude PURGES!!! CRAP STICKS!! my stomach just SANK... well i pulled him through the 5 lanes of the intersection then he was <B>GONE</B> i met him at the Conoco at the next light... he was laughing... i ask him how much of a shot he was running he showed me the .062 n2o and .050 fuel jets he was running  for those not familier with nitrous thats like a 200 shot on a 400cu.in.!!! he claimed the car makes 340hp at the wheels off the bottle and "a bit over 550hp squeezing"  so yeah i guess ya never know... but D@MN!!! it was like i wasn't even trying as he SCREAMED by me. oh well.. at least he was a decent guy. he had time slips from Commerece drag way running 10.9@124!!  i guess i never realized how much a difference 2 seconds really is at that speed! <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstmeatsig.jpg"> <BR> <BR>www.engineered.net<BR>Fast & Furious? Not really. More like moderately quick and slightly ticked off...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Kasdan||09-06-2001||09:13 AM||||well sh!t man, that sux, i think he was just messing with ya that first run.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||09-06-2001||09:30 AM||||Hey, I wouldn't feel terrible about it.  He was probably thinking the 400 cubes alone would be enough - "why waste nitrous running against a little orange Fiero," right?<P>Man, 400cu with a 200 shot of N2O!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000003||1FST2M6||09-06-2001||09:35 AM||||yeah thats what he said.. "i never would have guess that little thing giving me the run it did" he runs 13.5-13.1 all motor.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  it's nice to know i can rattle the cage of good ole american Torque! most of the street stangs and the camaros around here  are just noise... a few S/C but still not many can hook up... the 4cyl cars are just a waste of my gas so i don't bother with most of em.  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
